 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "Full Actors-pattern implementation (Governor + MarketEntry-LLM mock advisor + langgraph-clj StateGraph + append-only audit ledger + MemStore/DatomicStore), adapted from the cloud-itonami-iso3166-ago reference implementation: src/marketentry/{facts,governor,registry,store,marketentryllm,operation,phase}.cljc + full test suite (governor contract, store contract MemStore≡DatomicStore parity, registry pure-function, phase, integration StateGraph end-to-end for both a commit path and a hold path) + docs/business-model.md + docs/operator-guide.md. The jurisdiction dossier (marketentry.facts) is intentionally THINNER and more conservative than sibling jurisdictions (e.g. AGO): extensive research found no independently-verifiable named public-procurement regulator and no verified national e-procurement portal for São Tomé and Príncipe, so :owner-authority and :national-spec say so honestly rather than inventing either, the governor is SIX checks (not AGO's seven -- no analog of AGO's nif-unverified check, since the dossier does not ground a distinct STP tax-ID scheme), and the demo engagement set is 4 engagements (not AGO's 6). This also corrects this repo's original scaffold, which claimed an unverifiable named regulator (\"ARMP\") for São Tomé and Príncipe specifically -- that claim has been removed from facts.cljc, organization.edn, README.md and docs/ and replaced with only what is independently verified: Lei nº 8/2009 (procurement legal basis) and DGRN/Guiché Único para Empresas (commercial registration authority)."}
